": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1b4bd49ff58f83288a28d9a279ed6aba70088210f3135c070b26d88297bdf103","event_uuid":"5f5e4583-991c-43ee-9751-714f0ba8f162","position":{"commit_sha":"e1c96e85746ba548fc0d02095ccbfef9db632301","position":"1786913144351601001-5f5e4583-991c-43ee-9751-714f0ba8f162"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d17c277a4d0ccf21fb7f8eacdb40703dc980a227669cc99e717a793b13502fb5","event_uuid":"5788c443-ff5f-45f5-97ce-9980fa54e47e","position":{"commit_sha":"4d57cd8cbde356d30c9218a96789d3a86132a9ff","position":"1786913343365007001-5788c443-ff5f-45f5-97ce-9980fa54e47e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Additional evidence from lead-unpleasing-kitten: `test_ran_and_skipped_coexist_in_one_run` says its skipped record represents absent scc/lizard, but on this host scc 3.7.0 is present and the test still passes because unrelated inapplicable detectors contribute skipped records. Therefore it does not prove metric present or metric absent behavior. The deterministic metric-absence nodes do force `_METRIC_CANDIDATES`, so absence accounting remains covered; the new positive metric oracle must assert the backend and detector id explicitly.","timestamp":1786911603437863001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## PHASE 1 EXIT — proven root cause (rebar-debug fast path)\n\nRuntime reproduction on scc 3.7.0 traced the actual production call in `src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke`:\n\n- argv executed: `['/opt/homebrew/bin/scc', '--format', 'json', '.']`\n- parsed `Files` counts: 27 language groups, all zero\n- `_run_metric` result: `[]`, even though the repository contains files above the shipped 800-code-line cutoff\n- counterfactual with the same binary and input plus `--by-file`: 2,912 per-file entries, 29 with `Code > 800`\n\nConfirmed root cause: `_metric_invoke` omits scc's `--by-file` option at `engine_b_backends.py:376`. scc therefore emits only language summaries with empty `Files` arrays. `_scc_files` at lines 429-436 correctly consumes only per-file entries and consequently yields none; the threshold loop at lines 412-425 never executes and no metric match can be emitted. The only plausible alternative—that parsing or threshold comparison rejects otherwise-present entries—is ruled out by passing the same binary's `--by-file` JSON through `_scc_files`, which produced the expected 2,912 entries and 29 over-cutoff candidates.\n\nLegitimacy: `defect`. `src/rebar/grounding/detectors/builtin/smell_metric_oversize.yaml` authoritatively says `oversize_loc` flags files over a LOC cutoff, while `engine_b_backends.py:339-344` promises a present metric binary emits a match per file over the cutoff. Current behavior violates both contracts. Closed bug `rapid-cuboid-velvetcrab` independently established the same scc output contract for the metrics adapter and explicitly identified grounding `_scc_files` as a separate consumer.\n\nCaller-dependency gate: expected post-fix behavior is that a present scc invocation yields normalized matches for every returned file whose `Code` exceeds the configured cutoff, while below-cutoff files and all existing fail-open paths remain unchanged. The bounded caller sweep found `_metric_invoke` called only by `_run_metric`; that runner is dispatched through Engine B scan and then the grounding oracle. These callers consume evidence records and contractually expect matches, not an empty result. No behavioral dependency on the defect exists.\n\nFast-path criteria: deterministic reproduction, one directly observed mechanism, and a one-argument localized/reversible repair all hold. Phase 2 is unlocked after current plan review.","timestamp":1786913144351601001}],"created_at":1786910974260071001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"053f0e02-24db-4287-981a-0c18eccb0d43","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7da8-9d47-9604-4257"},{"link_uuid":"ccb7113b-9be5-4af5-9781-080c8b23455a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"01d4-1263-460a-416d"}],"description":"## Context\nThe Engine B metric backend parses per-file entries from scc JSON, but `_metric_invoke` invokes `scc --format json <repo>` without `--by-file`. With maintained scc 3.7.0, the language summary includes `Files: []` unless `--by-file` is requested. Therefore a present scc process can run successfully while `rebar.builtin.smell.metric-oversize` sees no files and can never emit its documented over-800-LOC matches.\n\nThe analogous code-health adapter defect was fixed by closed bug rapid-cuboid-velvetcrab, whose history explicitly notes grounding `_scc_files` is a separate consumer. Current coverage-reconstruction tests use a 50-LOC fixture or force tool absence, so they do not exercise the positive metric threshold path.\n\n## Reproduction\n- Run `scc --format json tests/unit/grounding` and inspect each language `Files` array: it is empty.\n- Compare with `scc --by-file --format json tests/unit/grounding`: per-file entries are present.\n- Inspect `src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke`: its command omits `--by-file` while `_scc_files` depends on `Files`.\n\n## Plan\n- Use rebar-debug to reproduce with a real scc binary and an over-800-code-line fixture, then prove the exact argv cause before editing.\n- Add a physically withheld RED oracle that observes a real or argv-faithful scc boundary and fails when `--by-file` is absent.\n- Correct the grounding metric invocation without changing thresholds or fail-open semantics.\n- Add positive match, below-threshold no-match, invalid-output, nonzero-exit, and tool-absent coverage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A present scc run over a file above the configured LOC threshold emits a normalized metric match for that file.\n- [ ] A present scc run below the threshold emits no fabricated match.\n- [ ] The scc command requests per-file JSON explicitly; checked by an argv-sensitive test.\n- [ ] Tool absence, timeout/nonzero failure, and invalid JSON remain fail-open evidence outcomes.\n- [ ] The focused grounding backend tests pass with the held-out exact-defect oracle.\n\n## Verification\n- Run the focused grounding metric tests with the worktree virtualenv.\n- Run the repository lint and typecheck gates.\n- Run the default test suite before landing through Gerrit.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py","reason":"correct scc argv to request per-file JSON"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py","reason":"add metric present-path and argv-sensitive regression coverage"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","01d4-1263-460a-416d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"36f63848-d941-4a95-95ca-af4042576661","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["grounding","bug","scc"],"ticket_id":"0024-fa99-d5bb-49bc","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Grounding metric detector omits scc --by-file and can never emit file matches","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["98373b2c-e7d9-4304-ad03-e442975c73ac","053f0e02-24db-4287-981a-0c18eccb0d43","967f7130-8114-4f66-b446-4276a38c3966","78e7f148-662c-4623-837d-b4395f47fdb4","36f63848-d941-4a95-95ca-af4042576661","203a7062-abe0-4afe-b5e5-9ee106a71210","ccb7113b-9be5-4af5-9781-080c8b23455a","5f5e4583-991c-43ee-9751-714f0ba8f162","5788c443-ff5f-45f5-97ce-9980fa54e47e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786913343365007002,"uuid":"8bf1ce72-3052-4092-9340-f80e7a74889e"}